            <ArticleTitle>A case of giant aneurysm following percutaneous coronary intervention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>731-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The incidence of restenosis has significantly reduced following introduction of drug-eluting stents. However. complications i.e. subacute thrombosis and aneurysm formation may be higher with these stents. We report a case of giant aneurysm formation following drug-eluting stent implantation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
